    "text": {
     "en": "After the Mauryas, many kingdoms rose. In the south the Cholas, Cheras and Pandyas ruled, and the Satavahanas ruled the Deccan.\nPorts on the coast traded pepper, pearls, cotton and spices with Rome and South-East Asia.\nSangam literature in Tamil describes life, love and war in the early Tamil kingdoms."
